      "code": "stun_attr_ref sar = stun_attr_get_first_by_type_str(buf, len, STUN_ATTRIBUTE_MESSAGE_INTEGRITY);",
      "note": "First project-code statement that parses the attacker-controlled STUN buffer, searching for a MESSAGE_INTEGRITY attribute using the corrupted buffer length. The attribute at offset 20 (type 0x0008, length 20) is found because the corrupted len makes the bounds check in stun_get_command_message_len_str vacuously pass.",
